From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:11:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Align computed calc values for Taffy's tagged pointers

Taffy's CompactLength keeps its tag in the low three bits of a pointer to the calc value. On wasm32 the struct only asked for 4-byte alignment, which held only because dlmalloc rounds every chunk to 8; an allocator that honours the requested alignment failed Taffy's assertion and left calc() insets unresolved.

Signed-off-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
---
 values/computed/length_percentage.rs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/values/computed/length_percentage.rs b/values/computed/length_percentage.rs
index cc5b853..2b52955 100644
--- a/values/computed/length_percentage.rs
+++ b/values/computed/length_percentage.rs
@@ -571,7 +571,9 @@ pub type CalcNode = calc::GenericCalcNode<ComputedLeaf>;
     ToCss,
     ToTyped,
 )]
-#[repr(C)]
+// Taffy's CompactLength keeps a tag in the low three bits of a pointer to this, so it must be
+// 8-aligned on 32-bit targets too rather than relying on the allocator rounding up.
+#[repr(C, align(8))]
 pub struct CalcLengthPercentage {
     #[animation(constant)]
     #[css(skip)]
